From: WFI-037 step (a) — add the 31 unprotected enforcement-chain scripts
Subject: [PATCH] fix(guard): protect the chain scripts the suffix list omitted

Human-applied patch. Both files are protected gate artifacts, so an agent may
stage this diff but may not apply it. See docs/workflow-improvements/WFI-037.md.

Apply with:
    git apply reports/notes/wfi-037a-guard-protected-coverage.patch
    python3 plugins/sdd-quality-loop/scripts/generate-guard-invariants.py

The regeneration step is REQUIRED. The guard reads the four generated modules,
not the JSON; without it the patch changes nothing at runtime. A further step is
required before the fix is live on this machine: the executing guard is the
installed copy under ~/.claude/plugins/cache/sdd-plugins/sdd-quality-loop/1.10.0/,
which lags the repository by 10 suffixes. Refresh the installed plugin or the
running guard keeps its old list.

WHY TWO FILES. The JSON is not the source of truth. The generator validates it
against a union computed from its own constants and rejects any divergence:

    if tuple(protected) != expected_protected:
        raise ValueError("protected_gate_suffixes must be the exact baseline/inventory union")
    # generate-guard-invariants.py:196-197

A JSON-only edit therefore fails the generator outright — verified, that is
exactly what a first draft of this patch did. The additions go into
BASELINE_SUFFIXES, and the JSON must mirror them at the position the union
places them: at the end of the baseline block, before the PHASE2 entries, not at
the end of the array.

Scope: step (a) of WFI-037's Proposed Change only — the 31 explicit additions
measured in ## Problem Evidence. Step (b) (inverting the file policy to
directory-default-protected with an exception list) and the shell
write-vocabulary widening are NOT in this patch. Step (a) closes the measured
coverage gap but not the drift that produced it.

